today we had a few items quite important  on our agenda we started by presenting  the priorities of creation presidency  later on Commission also presented three  new documents with a V European semester  and we had two topics which took quite I  would say constructive and Tauro  dialogue discussion one on the European  Grid deal with specific focus on  European Green Deal investment plan and  the last topic was our continuation of a  debate and discussion on the topic of  taxation with specific emphasis of  digital taxation today we heard a strong  support and commitments from finance  ministers to take ownership of the green  transition we share the views that each  country has its own challenges and  different starting points and the  Commission takes these different points  into account in its work it is also  clear that private capital will how to  cover the biggest part of transition  costs this is why one of my top  priorities is to drive forward our  sustainable finance agenda and bring  private investors on board ministers  also stressed the necessity for  international cooperation in this field  because EU is not the biggest polluter  this is why we already launched  international platform for sustainable  finance to work with other countries and  greening as a global financial system  and we are now reaching out for more  countries to join  moving to the digital taxation we are  heading now for a crucial moment of  reform of international corporate tax  system we have seen some progress as  oacd  on the first strand of reforms also  called a pillar one but we need to make  sure that these reforms are meaningful  when businesses are active in  jurisdictions without physical presence  this activity has to be captured  effectively we're more concerned at the  lack of parallel progress on minimum  effective taxation measures or pillar  two this is fundamental ensuring that  all businesses pay a fair share of tax  so today we called in you finance  ministers to speak with one voice  internationally on this you must be  active in the design of the global  solution to make sure among other things  that it worked for us both in terms of  fairness and competitiveness on a 10th  of January your country should all how  transpose the fifths anti-money  laundering directive these are wider  rules to ensure the integrity of the  Union financial system but I'm concerned  that quite a few of member states shall  not transpose them yet and there are no  two ways about it these rules must be  implemented in full and in timely way so  we will not be sitting idle here our  proposed to initiate infringement  proceedings against countries lagging  behind as early as in February
 

